proposed_comments.body:
### Use the windowless-safe clipboard API

**Severity:** `high`

`ClipboardHelper` is explicitly intended for extensions without a foreground window, but `Clipboard.SetContent(DataPackage)` is documented to throw unless the application is foreground or a debugger is attached. Command Palette extensions are activated as COM local servers, so `SetContent`/`SetImage` can fail in the background case this helper targets; this call also bypasses `ExecuteOnStaThread`'s `false`-result retries. Use `SetContentWithOptions`, retry its `false` result, and surface exhaustion while preserving `Flush` after success.

```suggestion
        var succeeded = false;
        ExecuteOnStaThread(() =>
        {
            succeeded = Clipboard.SetContentWithOptions(content, new ClipboardContentOptions());
            if (succeeded)
            {
                Clipboard.Flush();
            }

            return succeeded;
        });
        if (!succeeded)
        {
            throw new InvalidOperationException("Failed to set clipboard content.");
        }
```

### Surface exhausted text writes (1/3)

**Severity:** `medium`

`SetClipboardData` returns `false` when a native clipboard operation fails, and `ExecuteOnStaThread` retries that result but discards the final outcome. This call therefore returns normally after all attempts fail, so an extension can report a successful copy while the clipboard was not updated. Capture the delegate's final result and throw or otherwise surface failure after the retries; apply it with the RTF and caught-failure suggestions.

```suggestion
        var succeeded = false;
        ExecuteOnStaThread(() => succeeded = SetClipboardData(Tuple.Create(text, CF_UNICODETEXT)));
        if (!succeeded)
        {
            throw new InvalidOperationException("Failed to set clipboard text.");
        }
```

### Surface exhausted RTF writes (2/3)

**Severity:** `medium`

The RTF path has the same lost-result behavior as `SetText`: `SetClipboardData` can return `false` after the bounded retries, but this public method still completes normally. Preserve and check the final delegate result so callers can distinguish a completed write from a failed or partial text/RTF update. Apply it together with the paired text and caught-failure suggestions.

```suggestion
        var succeeded = false;
        ExecuteOnStaThread(() => succeeded = SetClipboardData(
            Tuple.Create(plainText, CF_UNICODETEXT),
            Tuple.Create(rtfText, s_CF_RTF)));
        if (!succeeded)
        {
            throw new InvalidOperationException("Failed to set clipboard RTF.");
        }
```
